cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If Project Magnolia contributes to work you publish, please cite the
  repository as below, naming the commit or tag you actually used.
title: "Project Magnolia: an agentic research assistant for computational chemistry"
abstract: >-
  Project Magnolia is a conversational research assistant for computational
  chemistry. It drives pocket prediction, docking, molecular dynamics, quantum
  chemistry and generative design on a workstation or a Slurm cluster, and keeps
  a reviewable laboratory notebook of what was run, what resulted, and what was
  learnt. Observations that recur across sessions are proposed for promotion into
  version-controlled standing rules, subject to the researcher's approval.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/HolobiomicsLab/Magnolia-AI"
license-url: "https://github.com/HolobiomicsLab/Magnolia-AI/blob/master/LICENSE"
keywords:
  - computational chemistry
  - agentic AI
  - molecular docking
  - quantum chemistry
  - molecular dynamics
  - laboratory notebook
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
  - Model Context Protocol
